diff --git a/features/todo-completion.feature b/features/todo-completion.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..e8107f7
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/todo-completion.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,76 @@
+Feature: Todo completion
+  As a user
+  I want to mark todos as complete and manage completed items
+  So that I can track my progress
+
+  Rule: Toggle single todo
+
+  Scenario: Mark a todo as completed by clicking its checkbox
+    Given the app is loaded with a single active todo "Buy groceries"
+    When I click the toggle checkbox for "Buy groceries"
+    Then the todo "Buy groceries" has the completed class
+    And its toggle checkbox is checked
+
+  Scenario: Reopen a completed todo by clicking its checkbox
+    Given the app is loaded with a single completed todo "Buy groceries"
+    When I click the toggle checkbox for "Buy groceries"
+    Then the todo "Buy groceries" does not have the completed class
+    And its toggle checkbox is not checked
+
+  Rule: Toggle all
+
+  Scenario: Mark all todos as complete via the toggle-all checkbox
+    Given the app is loaded with 2 active todos "Buy groceries" and "Walk the dog"
+    When I click the toggle-all checkbox
+    Then both todos have the completed class
+    And the toggle-all checkbox is checked
+
+  Scenario: Mark all todos as active when toggle-all is unchecked
+    Given the app is loaded with 2 completed todos "Buy groceries" and "Walk the dog"
+    When I click the toggle-all checkbox
+    Then neither todo has the completed class
+    And the toggle-all checkbox is not checked
+
+  Scenario: Toggle-all reflects state when a single todo is toggled
+    Given the app is loaded with active todos "Buy groceries" and "Walk the dog"
+    When I click the toggle checkbox for "Buy groceries"
+    Then the toggle-all checkbox is not checked
+
+  Rule: Clear completed button
+
+  Scenario: Remove all completed todos with Clear completed
+    Given the app is loaded with a completed todo "Buy groceries" and an active todo "Walk the dog"
+    When I click the Clear completed button
+    Then the todo list contains 1 item with title "Walk the dog"
+    And "Buy groceries" is not in the todo list
+
+  Scenario: Clear completed button is hidden when there are no completed todos
+    Given the app is loaded with an active todo "Buy groceries"
+    Then the Clear completed button is hidden
+
+  Scenario: Clear completed button is visible when there is at least one completed todo
+    Given the app is loaded with a completed todo "Buy groceries"
+    Then the Clear completed button is visible
+
+  Rule: Active count
+
+  Scenario: Display the count of active todos
+    Given the app is loaded with a completed todo "Buy groceries" and an active todo "Walk the dog"
+    Then the todo count shows "1 item left"
+
+  Scenario: Pluralize item count correctly
+    Given the app is loaded with no persisted todos
+    When I type "Buy groceries" into the new-todo input and press Enter
+    Then the todo count shows "1 item left"
+    When I type "Walk the dog" into the new-todo input and press Enter
+    Then the todo count shows "2 items left"
+
+  Scenario: Update count when a todo is completed
+    Given the app is loaded with active todos "Buy groceries" and "Walk the dog"
+    When I click the toggle checkbox for "Buy groceries"
+    Then the todo count shows "1 item left"
+
+  Scenario: Update count after Clear completed
+    Given the app is loaded with a completed todo "Buy groceries" and an active todo "Walk the dog"
+    When I click the Clear completed button
+    Then the todo count shows "1 item left"
\ No newline at end of file
diff --git a/features/todo-editing.feature b/features/todo-editing.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..cc0de66
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/todo-editing.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,68 @@
+Feature: Todo editing
+  As a user
+  I want to edit the title of an existing todo
+  So that I can correct or update my tasks
+
+  Rule: Activate editing
+
+  Scenario: Double-click a todo label to enter editing mode
+    Given the app is loaded with a single active todo "Buy groceries"
+    When I double-click the label for "Buy groceries"
+    Then the todo "Buy groceries" has the editing class
+    And the edit input contains "Buy groceries"
+
+  Scenario: Edit input is focused when editing mode is activated
+    Given the app is loaded with a single active todo "Buy groceries"
+    When I double-click the label for "Buy groceries"
+    Then the edit input for "Buy groceries" has focus
+
+  Rule: Save edits
+
+  Scenario: Save edit by pressing Enter
+    Given the app is loaded with a single active todo "Buy groceries"
+    When I double-click the label for "Buy groceries"
+    And I change the edit input to "Buy organic groceries" and press Enter
+    Then the todo list contains 1 item with title "Buy organic groceries"
+    And the todo "Buy organic groceries" does not have the editing class
+
+  Scenario: Save edit by blurring the edit input
+    Given the app is loaded with a single active todo "Buy groceries"
+    When I double-click the label for "Buy groceries"
+    And I change the edit input to "Buy organic groceries" and blur it
+    Then the todo list contains 1 item with title "Buy organic groceries"
+    And the todo "Buy organic groceries" does not have the editing class
+
+  Scenario: Trim whitespace on save
+    Given the app is loaded with a single active todo "Buy groceries"
+    When I double-click the label for "Buy groceries"
+    And I change the edit input to "   Buy organic groceries   " and press Enter
+    Then the todo list contains 1 item with title "Buy organic groceries"
+
+  Rule: Cancel editing
+
+  Scenario: Cancel edit by pressing Escape
+    Given the app is loaded with a single active todo "Buy groceries"
+    When I double-click the label for "Buy groceries"
+    And I change the edit input to "Buy organic groceries" and press Escape
+    Then the todo list contains 1 item with title "Buy groceries"
+
+  Rule: Delete on empty
+
+  Scenario: Delete todo when edit input is emptied and saved
+    Given the app is loaded with a single active todo "Buy groceries"
+    When I double-click the label for "Buy groceries"
+    And I change the edit input to "" and press Enter
+    Then the todo list is empty
+
+  Scenario: Delete todo when edit input is whitespace-only and saved
+    Given the app is loaded with a single active todo "Buy groceries"
+    When I double-click the label for "Buy groceries"
+    And I change the edit input to "   " and press Enter
+    Then the todo list is empty
+
+  Rule: Destroy button
+
+  Scenario: Remove a todo by clicking the destroy button
+    Given the app is loaded with a single active todo "Buy groceries"
+    When I click the destroy button for "Buy groceries"
+    Then the todo list is empty
\ No newline at end of file
diff --git a/features/todo-management.feature b/features/todo-management.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..f01bac0
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/todo-management.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,44 @@
+Feature: Todo management
+  As a user
+  I want to create and view todos
+  So that I can track what needs to be done
+
+  Rule: New todos
+
+  Scenario: Create a new todo by pressing Enter
+    Given the app is loaded with no persisted todos
+    When I type "Buy groceries" into the new-todo input and press Enter
+    Then the todo list contains 1 item with title "Buy groceries"
+    And the new-todo input is cleared
+
+  Scenario: Trim whitespace from the todo title
+    Given the app is loaded with no persisted todos
+    When I type "   Walk the dog   " into the new-todo input and press Enter
+    Then the todo list contains 1 item with title "Walk the dog"
+
+  Scenario: Do not create a todo for empty input
+    Given the app is loaded with no persisted todos
+    When I type "" into the new-todo input and press Enter
+    Then the todo list is empty
+
+  Scenario: Do not create a todo for whitespace-only input
+    Given the app is loaded with no persisted todos
+    When I type "   " into the new-todo input and press Enter
+    Then the todo list is empty
+
+  Scenario: New-todo input is focused on page load
+    Given the app is loaded with no persisted todos
+    Then the new-todo input has focus
+
+  Rule: No-todos state
+
+  Scenario: Hide main and footer when there are no todos
+    Given the app is loaded with no persisted todos
+    Then the main section is hidden
+    And the footer is hidden
+
+  Scenario: Show main and footer when there is at least one todo
+    Given the app is loaded with no persisted todos
+    When I type "Buy groceries" into the new-todo input and press Enter
+    Then the main section is visible
+    And the footer is visible
\ No newline at end of file
diff --git a/features/todo-persistence.feature b/features/todo-persistence.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..fbdf358
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/todo-persistence.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,51 @@
+Feature: Todo persistence
+  As a user
+  I want my todos to be saved across page reloads
+  So that I do not lose my tasks
+
+  Rule: localStorage save
+
+  Scenario: Save todos to localStorage on creation
+    Given the app is loaded with no persisted todos
+    When I type "Buy groceries" into the new-todo input and press Enter
+    Then localStorage contains a todo with title "Buy groceries" and completed false
+
+  Scenario: Save todos to localStorage on completion toggle
+    Given the app is loaded with a single active todo "Buy groceries"
+    When I click the toggle checkbox for "Buy groceries"
+    Then localStorage contains a todo with title "Buy groceries" and completed true
+
+  Scenario: Remove todo from localStorage on deletion
+    Given the app is loaded with a single active todo "Buy groceries"
+    When I click the destroy button for "Buy groceries"
+    Then localStorage contains no todos
+
+  Scenario: Update todo title in localStorage on edit
+    Given the app is loaded with a single active todo "Buy groceries"
+    When I double-click the label for "Buy groceries"
+    And I change the edit input to "Buy organic groceries" and press Enter
+    Then localStorage contains a todo with title "Buy organic groceries" and completed false
+    And localStorage does not contain a todo with title "Buy groceries"
+
+  Scenario: Restore todos from localStorage on page load
+    Given localStorage has a persisted todo with title "Buy groceries" and completed false
+    When the app is loaded fresh
+    Then the todo list contains 1 item with title "Buy groceries"
+
+  Scenario: Restore completed state from localStorage
+    Given localStorage has a persisted todo with title "Buy groceries" and completed true
+    When the app is loaded fresh
+    Then the todo "Buy groceries" has the completed class
+
+  Scenario: Do not persist editing state
+    Given the app is loaded with a single active todo "Buy groceries"
+    When I double-click the label for "Buy groceries"
+    And I change the edit input to "Buy organic groceries" and press Enter
+    Then the persisted todo "Buy organic groceries" does not carry editing class state
+
+  Rule: localStorage key
+
+  Scenario: Use correct localStorage key
+    Given the app is loaded with no persisted todos
+    When I type "Buy groceries" into the new-todo input and press Enter
+    Then the localStorage key is "todos-javascript"
\ No newline at end of file
diff --git a/features/todo-routing.feature b/features/todo-routing.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..6484965
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/todo-routing.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,54 @@
+Feature: Todo routing
+  As a user
+  I want to filter the todo list by completion state
+  So that I can focus on active or completed items
+
+  Rule: Default route
+
+  Scenario: Show all todos by default
+    Given the app is loaded with an active todo "Buy groceries" and a completed todo "Walk the dog"
+    Then the todo list shows 2 items
+    And the All filter link has the selected class
+
+  Rule: Active filter
+
+  Scenario: Show only active todos when filtering by Active
+    Given the app is loaded with an active todo "Buy groceries" and a completed todo "Walk the dog"
+    When I click the Active filter link
+    Then the todo list shows 1 item with title "Buy groceries"
+    And the Active filter link has the selected class
+
+  Scenario: Update active filter when a todo is completed under Active view
+    Given the app is loaded with active todos "Buy groceries" and "Walk the dog"
+    When I click the Active filter link
+    And I click the toggle checkbox for "Buy groceries"
+    Then the todo list shows 1 item with title "Walk the dog"
+
+  Rule: Completed filter
+
+  Scenario: Show only completed todos when filtering by Completed
+    Given the app is loaded with an active todo "Buy groceries" and a completed todo "Walk the dog"
+    When I click the Completed filter link
+    Then the todo list shows 1 item with title "Walk the dog"
+    And the Completed filter link has the selected class
+
+  Rule: Route via URL hash
+
+  Scenario: Navigate to active filter via URL hash
+    Given the app is loaded with an active todo "Buy groceries" and a completed todo "Walk the dog"
+    When the URL hash is set to "#/active"
+    Then the todo list shows 1 item with title "Buy groceries"
+    And the Active filter link has the selected class
+
+  Scenario: Navigate to completed filter via URL hash
+    Given the app is loaded with an active todo "Buy groceries" and a completed todo "Walk the dog"
+    When the URL hash is set to "#/completed"
+    Then the todo list shows 1 item with title "Walk the dog"
+    And the Completed filter link has the selected class
+
+  Scenario: Navigate to all filter via URL hash
+    Given the app is loaded with an active todo "Buy groceries" and a completed todo "Walk the dog"
+    When the URL hash is set to "#/completed"
+    And the URL hash is set to "#/"
+    Then the todo list shows 2 items
+    And the All filter link has the selected class
\ No newline at end of file
